    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "This period residence with its associated outbuildings is set within 2.3 acres of well-established grounds located just 3 km from central Tralee. The elevated position of Listellick House is encircled by panoramic views of the Sliabh Mish mountains and, in the distance, Tralee Bay.\r\n\r\nThe main house, built in 1864, is a genuinely rare offering, an imposing period residence, approached via a sweeping gravelled driveway framed by mature trees and hedgerows that afford great privacy.\r\n\r\nThe interior of Listellick House more than lives up to the promise of its attractive elevation, with generously proportioned and well-lit rooms and associated period features, as well as the contemporary adaptations that have been made by the current owner to allow the property be enjoyed for a more contemporary way of family living and to take the best advantage of its surroundings.\r\n\r\nThe property is further distinguished by the addition of two substantial period outbuildings; a two-storey stone granary which offers enormous potential for conversion (subject to planning permission) into a studio, guest accommodation, home office, or additional living space, and a large stone storage building, ideal for equipment, workshop use, or further development. Together, these outbuildings add both character and practical flexibility.\r\n\r\nWithin the grounds there is a discreetly located floodlit tennis court which is ideal for private games or for entertaining friends and family.\r\n\r\nListellick House represents a rare chance to own a home of real historical substance and distinction. A truly exceptional opportunity to acquire a piece of Kerry's architectural heritage.\r\n\r\n           \r\nOUTSIDE\r\nMature grounds extending to C.2.35 acres\r\nOld Granary extending to C.85sq.m. over two floors.  Potential to convert (subject to planning permission) into a work from home space, studio, guest accommodation, additional living space or  family gym etc.\r\nTennis court: Tarmac surface and floodlit\r\nSouth westerly facing raised patio area off kitchen \r\nStone outhouse with enclosed dog run\r\nPrefabricated garden shed\r\n\r\nViewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate the scale, character, and setting of this exceptional property.\r\n\r\nNOTE: Potential to acquire an additional 8.9 acres"
      },
